00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:52.220
Well, but it was a costume, though.

689
00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:52.390
Oh, my God.

690
00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.400
It wasn't a regular day in character thing.

691
00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:55.180
That's what I'm saying.

692
00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:55.360
It doesn't apply.

693
00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:56.720
Am I talking to Jenna or Creed?

694
00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:57.640
I don't know anymore.

695
00:23:57.940 --> 00:23:58.260
It doesn't apply.

696
00:23:58.440 --> 00:23:58.820
All right.

697
00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:03.260
You know the scene where Pam and Jim set up a resume for Dwight to get a job someplace else?

698
00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:04.960
I have a fan question about that.

699
00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:11.760
RCJH asked, what were you typing on the computer when you and Jim were working on Dwight's resume?

700
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:14.120
I was typing what we were saying.

701
00:24:14.740 --> 00:24:16.060
Of course you were, Jenna.

702
00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:18.380
Of course you were, because you're so method.

703
00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:19.300
I was very method.

704
00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:20.540
You're like, I am a responsible person.

705
00:24:20.540 --> 00:24:23.500
You would type out your lines on the computer while you were doing it?

706
00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:27.120
Yeah, because Jim would say, I would say, what should we say here?

707
00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:30.860
And then he would say what we should say, and I would type it.

708
00:24:31.060 --> 00:24:32.320
And see, here's the thing.

709
00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.640
I'm very proud of my typing skills.

710
00:24:34.700 --> 00:24:35.240
Oh, we know.

711
00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:35.640
We know.

712
00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:36.000
Yeah.

713
00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:38.380
Creed, do we know or do we know?

714
00:24:38.480 --> 00:24:39.500
We really know.

715
00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:39.900
You guys.

716
00:24:39.900 --> 00:24:41.160
Now I'm back on your side, Angela.

717
00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:42.280
Thank you, Creed.

718
00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:44.060
Is this how it feels?

719
00:24:44.240 --> 00:24:44.420
Yes.

720
00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:45.300
Is this how it feels?

721
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:45.580
Yeah.

722
00:24:45.740 --> 00:24:46.120
We know.

723
00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:47.920
You'd walk in this thing with just your fingers.

724
00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:51.920
We'd be talking about stuff at a craft store, and your fingers would be going like you're typing.

725
00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:53.660
Oh, now that is not true.

726
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:54.260
It was too much.

727
00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:54.840
It was too much.

728
00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:56.400
Tone it down.

729
00:24:57.120 --> 00:25:00.660
And then you would tell us about your typing speed and your level of accuracy.

730
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:07.940
Well, you should know I was typing our actual lines.

731
00:25:08.020 --> 00:25:09.200
Well, I think that's pretty great, though.

732
00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:09.600
Because I can.

733
00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:11.880
Because she could, and I can, and I will.

734
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:12.800
And you're fast, too.

735
00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:13.340
That's right.

736
00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:13.840
She's very faSt.

737
00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:24.140
Because Michael's scene with Dwight, when he calls Dwight into his office, and he tells Dwight that he has to fire someone, and Dwight starts naming all the people he should fire.

738
00:25:24.140 --> 00:25:32.060
But then Michael implies maybe it should be Dwight, and then Michael's second head starts talking to Dwight.

739
00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:32.760
That's right.

740
00:25:32.760 --> 00:25:37.600
Do you remember Steve and Rain laughing during that scene?

741
00:25:37.600 --> 00:25:38.520
Because I do.

742
00:25:38.520 --> 00:25:40.800
I remember they could not get through that scene.

743
00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:46.880
I'm sitting out at reception in the background, and they were cracking themselves up in there.

744
00:25:46.960 --> 00:25:49.060
Rain was literally doubling over.

745
00:25:49.060 --> 00:25:52.460
Because he was kind of leaning forward, and he would just kind of collapse into himself.

746
00:25:52.460 --> 00:25:53.620
He was laughing so hard.

747
00:25:53.740 --> 00:25:55.840
There must be deleted scenes of that scene.

748
00:25:55.880 --> 00:25:56.640
Oh, man.

749
00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:57.040
I would love to see those.

750
00:25:57.040 --> 00:25:57.980
I would love to see that.

751
00:25:58.080 --> 00:25:58.240
Yeah.

752
00:25:58.360 --> 00:25:59.440
That is a funny scene.

753
00:25:59.620 --> 00:26:01.820
Well, Paul Feig called in when we did Office Olympics,

754
00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:09.100
and he said one of the things he loved about directing episodes of our shows is that you could really find a shot that was cool,

755
00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:13.000
and you would have the support of Greg to just kind of go with it.

756
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:22.020
And he sort of found that shot where Dwight as the Sith Lord has his, like, hood kind of like – it looks like it's straight out of the movie, you know?

757
00:26:22.220 --> 00:26:22.400
Yes.

758
00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:23.800
And they just loved that.

759
00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:24.780
The shot from the side, right?

760
00:26:24.780 --> 00:26:25.600
Yeah, shot from the side.

761
00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:25.720
Yeah.

762
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:31.480
And they sort of just found that and went with it, and Greg was totally supportive of it, and Paul was talking about, like,

763
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:35.820
how fun that was to have that creative freedom and find those little nuggets.

764
00:26:35.820 --> 00:26:37.160
And it's so cool looking.

765
00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:38.860
We had a lot of shots like that.

766
00:26:38.940 --> 00:26:42.200
They just weren't the cookie-cutter or stereotype, you know, sitcom stuff.

767
00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:43.920
And we'd get interesting shots at times.

768
00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:44.160
Yeah.

769
00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:46.020
Because all the cameramen were so great.

770
00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:50.880
And something that we haven't talked about on the show yet is the idea of actor marks.

771
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:58.660
So usually on a television show, so that they can get these shots, they put a little piece of tape on the ground.

772
00:26:58.660 --> 00:27:05.800
And if you – for example, if Jim had to walk up to Pam's desk, there would be a little mark on the ground, and he would have to stand exactly on that mark.

773
00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:07.020
And it's really hard to do.

774
00:27:07.140 --> 00:27:08.360
I mean, do you guys find it hard to do?

775
00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:14.060
I'm always – I feel like I'm always looking down for the tape, and then I get to my spot, and I look up.

776
00:27:14.120 --> 00:27:15.820
It's, like, a hard thing to manage.

